<title>SINGAPORE: CAM former director charged - CAD.</title>
<headline>CAM former director charged - CAD.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>CAM International's former managing director and chief executive Raymond Chew was charged on Saturday with misappropriating S$1.45 million of company funds, a spokeswoman for the Commercial Affairs Department (CAD) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Straits Times newspaper reported that Chew had been released from custody on S$1.5 million bail.</p>
<p>The paper said Chew had given the CAD all his travel documents and that the next court hearing would be on July 18.</p>
<p>Precision engineering company CAM International is at the centre of investigation by the CAD for alleged fraud.</p>
<p>Trading of the company's shares has been suspended.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080</p>
